# BATS_doppler_run_template.sbatch
Template for running BATS in HPC
Currently has variables allowing it to be template for running BATS_wrapper.sh or BATS_input.sh

# BATS_wrapper.sh
Allows you to input batch of dates into BATS
Uses a dependency so the next date can only run once the one before it has finished running
If a date fails, the rest of the dates cannot run
Input of dates, output of classified files

#BATS_input.sh
Also allows you to input batch of dates into BATS
Doesn't use a dependency, so sometimes files run at the same time and become a single classified file

#geotif_crop.sh
Template for running outputted classified files from BATS and generates tsv files
Currently has variables allowing it to be template for running crop_input.sh
Additionally crops to 500m surrounding causeway

#crop_input.sh
Allows you to run batch of dates
Requires BATS to have been fully run before using
Input of classified files, output of tsv files

#save_to_local.sh
Allows you to save batches of tsv files generated in crop_input.sh to local computer

#make_covell_fullframe_box_v16_newcenter.py
Generates videos from tif files
Takes tif files from within the classified folder generated by BATS and turns it into a video with colors and a roadmap overlayed
Input of classified files, output of tif files with map overlay and mp4 video

# coords.csv
Coordinates directly surrounding the 1-80 Causeway
The three pixels directly North and South of the midline of the causeway
Coordinates selected used Google Earth Pro
C=Center, W=West, E=East
Used in Load and Create Dataframes.R

# sunset_times.csv
Sunset times from 2013 to 2025
Generated using https://gml.noaa.gov/grad/solcalc/calcdetails.html
Used in BATS_doppler_run_template.sbatch
